一、概要
摘要：随着在线业务规模的持续增长，分布式关系型数据库集群逐渐成为支撑高并发与海量数据的重要基础设施。然而在实际生产环境中，异构数据库迁移、集群在线扩缩容以及端到端数据一致性校验仍然面临较大挑战：现有工具多面向单机数据库，缺乏对分片规则的感知，扩容往往需要停机或长时间维护窗口，难以满足关键业务对连续性的要求。本文面向分布式关系型数据库集群，设计并实现了一套支持全量迁移与基于变更日志增量同步的数据库迁移与弹性扩缩容系统。系统采用输入层、核心服务层、插件适配层和 Web 管理层的分层架构，通过标准复制协议捕获源库变更日志，将其解析为内部事件模型，并结合集群分片算法完成 Slot 级路由与并行写入。基于此，本文提出了一种由“全量快照迁移—增量日志追赶—基于控制节点元数据锁的路由切换”构成的在线重分片机制，实现了节点级扩缩容过程中的低感知数据搬迁。同时，系统实现了基于“伪从库”思想的非侵入式数据校验模块，以及覆盖任务配置、生命周期管理、拓扑展示和实时监控的 Web 可视化界面，有效降低了复杂迁移与扩缩容任务的运维成本。
Abstract: With the rapid growth of online business, distributed relational database clusters have become a common solution to support high concurrency and large-scale data. However, in real-world production environments, enterprises still face significant challenges in heterogeneous data migration, online scaling of distributed clusters, and end-to-end data consistency validation. Traditional migration tools are usually oriented to single-node databases, lack awareness of sharding rules, and often require long maintenance windows or downtime during capacity expansion, which is difficult to accept for core business systems. This thesis designs and implements a data migration and synchronization system for distributed relational database clusters, combining full snapshot loading with log-based incremental replication to support elastic scaling. The proposed system adopts a layered architecture comprising an input layer for change data capture, a server layer for scheduling and flow control, a plugin layer for heterogeneous target adaptation, and a Web-based administration layer for visual management. At the core, the system connects to source databases via standard replication protocols, parses binary logs into an internal event model, and, by integrating the sharding algorithm of the distributed cluster, performs slot-level routing to the appropriate storage nodes. On this basis, the thesis further proposes an online resharding mechanism for distributed database clusters. The mechanism combines parallel snapshot migration and incremental log replay, and introduces a three-phase switching protocol consisting of full data copy, incremental catch-up, and short-term metadata lock–based route switch at the control node. This design enables node-level scale-out and shard redistribution with minimal impact on foreground applications. In addition, a non-intrusive data verification module based on a "fake slave" idea is implemented to provide continuous or sampled consistency checking between source and target. A Web-based management console is developed to support task configuration, lifecycle management, topology visualization, and real-time monitoring, significantly reducing the operational complexity of complex migration and scaling tasks.
